# Build context hygiene. Everything here is either irrelevant to the image or
# student output that would make builds non-reproducible.

# macOS / editor noise
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
*~
*.swp

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Instructor-only - not shipped inside the student image
instructor/
INSTRUCTOR-TEST.md
RISK-GUIDE.md
publish.sh

# Host-side launcher scripts - students run these OUTSIDE the container
setup/

# Written at RUN time by the lab and never carried in from the context:
#   tamper-log.jsonl   the detect beat's log
#   server-state.json  which poison mode poison.py has armed
#   *-results.txt      the runner's saved transcript
#
# trust.json is NOT here. It is the shipped trust list the student drops from and
# re-pins, so it must be in the image. The Dockerfile COPYs it twice - once as
# itself and once as trust.default.json - so every run starts from the shipped
# state. Lab 13 hit exactly this with its policy file.
tamper-log.jsonl
server-state.json
*-results.txt

# Credentials
.env
*.pem
*.key
